      "id": "binary-ternary-and-rondo-form",
      "title": "Binary, Ternary, and Rondo Form",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** theory-advanced | **Difficulty:** 4/10 | **Time:** ~12 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Musical form describes how sections organise in time — from simple dance repeats to symphonic architecture."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "binary-ab",
      "title": "Binary (AB)",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Two complementary sections. Each may repeat: AABB. Baroque dances often binary. First section modulates to dominant; second returns home."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ternary-aba",
      "title": "Ternary (ABA)",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Statement, contrast, return. Minuet and trio: minuet A, trio B, minuet A. Da capo aria in opera. Three-part song form."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rondo",
      "title": "Rondo",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Refrain alternates with episodes: ABACA or ABACABA. Episodes provide contrast; refrain returns familiar. Finale movements often rondo."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sonata-form",
      "title": "Sonata form",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Large-scale: exposition (themes in tonic and dominant), development (fragment, modulate), recapitulation (themes in tonic). Extended ternary at symphonic scale."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trad-tunes",
      "title": "Trad tunes",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "AABB most common in reels and jigs. 32-bar song form (AABA) in jazz standards."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
